; Extension §4: a negated literal is never a generator, so `X` is used by
; `(not (q X))` with nothing before it able to bind it. Rejected at the variable
; — the alternative would be closed-world over a guessed sort.
;
; Both columns are declared so the file fails range restriction and nothing
; else: an untyped `q` would fail sort inference first and prove the wrong
; thing.

(relation r (person))
(relation q (person))

(rule (r X)
  (not (q X)))
